                <note rend="inline" type="source">384.11/174: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Cairo</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Richards</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-08T12:00:00+02:00">July 8, 1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        July 13—4:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Information received from British Consul, Gore, Abyssinia, through British
                    Residency Cairo, communications are restored Sudan Interior Mission at Jimma and
                    at Agaro and that all missionaries are safe.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richards</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
